# What:    Files git must not track in this repository.
# How:     Read automatically by git; also used by `node tools/cli.mjs lint-headers` (read-only
#          `git ls-files --others --ignored --exclude-standard`) to skip these files.
# Needs:   Nothing.
# Outputs: Run outputs, installed packages, runtime scratch and personal/secret files stay out of git.

# Run outputs (one folder per run; old v1 folders are evidence and stay untouched).
# Anchored with a leading "/" so it matches ONLY the root results/ folder: an unanchored `results/`
# would also hide tools/results/ (the JSON Schemas) and tools/report/unit-tests/fixtures/results/.
/results/
# A local copy of the first version (v1) and its archive spec, not shipped: the first version is on its
# own branch (docs/open-questions.md §2.6). Ignored so it can never be committed by accident.
/archive/
# Installed npm packages (npm install recreates them from package-lock.json)
node_modules/
# Runtime scratch of the tools (.cache/inspect/, .cache/plan-definitions/, …)
.cache/
# Personal environment overrides, deep-merged over config/environments/<env>.json
config/environments/*.local.json
# Monitoring secrets (copy of monitoring/.env.example with real values)
monitoring/.env
